{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>You shall not go back to take it… that HaShem your Elohim may bless you.</b> He fixed blessing in the gift of thought. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: ״למען יברכך״ — even though it came to his hand without intent, how much more so for one who does so with intent. Say from this: a shekel fell from his hand and a poor man found it and was sustained by it — he is blessed for it."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:50:51.685052971Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}